WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.408
The ship sank. Who pays for the loss?

00:00:03.458 --> 00:00:06.508
The answer is in three letters on your invoice.

00:00:06.558 --> 00:00:08.725
The Incoterm tells you two things:

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.978
who pays the freight and where the risk changes hands.

00:00:12.316 --> 00:00:14.437
Every import travels this path.

00:00:14.487 --> 00:00:16.794
Under EXW, you pick the goods up at the factory.

00:00:16.844 --> 00:00:19.046
The risk is yours from the factory door.

00:00:19.096 --> 00:00:21.473
Under FOB, the seller puts the cargo on board.

00:00:21.523 --> 00:00:24.108
From then on, freight and risk are yours.

00:00:24.158 --> 00:00:28.032
Under DDP, the seller delivers to your door, duties paid.

00:00:28.082 --> 00:00:29.484
Now, the catch.

00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:32.655
Under CIF, the seller pays the freight to Santos.

00:00:32.819 --> 00:00:35.754
So the risk is the seller's until Santos, right?

00:00:36.454 --> 00:00:37.367
Wrong.

00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:38.737
The risk passed to you

00:00:38.787 --> 00:00:41.280
when the cargo went on board, back in China.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:44.612
The ship sank at sea? The loss is yours.

00:00:44.662 --> 00:00:46.911
What covers it is the insurance that comes with CIF.

00:00:46.961 --> 00:00:49.256
Read the Incoterm before the price.

00:00:49.306 --> 00:00:52.299
Comment INCOTERM and I'll send you the table with all eleven.
